		<descript>
			<abstract>This digital dataset represents the geologic map symbols of the Smoky Mountain 30' x 60' quadrangle, Kane and San Juan Counties, Utah, and Coconino County, Arizona.  Doelling originally mapped this area as part of a major study of Kane County during 1983 to 1989 (Doelling and Davis, 1989). The UGS digitized this dataset from a copy of the eastern part of the 1:100,000-scale "Geologic Map of Kane County, Utah" by Hellmut H. Doelling and Fitzhugh D. Davis, published by the Utah Geological (and Mineral) Survey in 1989 as Map 121, which was revised and hand drafted by the lead author, with minor additions from other sources.  Significant modifications were made by the authors in 2005 using 1:24,000-scale color aerial photographs with limited field verification.  The most significant modifications were to map the Page Sandstone across the map area and to modify contacts near the Lake Powell shoreline.  On parts of the source map (UGS Map 121) the Page Sandstone is included with the Navajo Sandstone and Carmel Formation.  Data is for use at scales not to exceed 1:100,000.</abstract>
			<purpose>To provide basic geologic data in digital format for government, academic, and public users.</purpose>
			<langdata Sync="TRUE">en</langdata>
		</descript>
